1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,447
A kite drifts across the sky.

2
00:00:02,447 --> 00:00:04,299
A ball curves to a friend.

3
00:00:04,299 --> 00:00:06,393
A bicycle swings around a bend.

4
00:00:06,793 --> 00:00:08,788
None moves in a straight line.

5
00:00:08,788 --> 00:00:11,369
So how do we describe motion that bends?

6
00:00:11,819 --> 00:00:14,720
Aarav cuts across an
empty road at a slant.

7
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:18,214
Each second, four metres
east and three metres north.

8
00:00:18,564 --> 00:00:21,218
So is he going seven metres per second?

9
00:00:21,218 --> 00:00:22,693
Most people say yes.

10
00:00:22,693 --> 00:00:23,861
They are wrong.

11
00:00:24,361 --> 00:00:28,198
By the end, you will know his real
speed, and the trick behind it.

12
00:00:28,848 --> 00:00:30,124
First, where is he?

13
00:00:30,124 --> 00:00:32,550
On a straight road, one number was enough.

14
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:34,934
On flat ground, we need two.

15
00:00:34,934 --> 00:00:36,273
x, how far east.

16
00:00:36,273 --> 00:00:37,911
And y, how far north.

17
00:00:38,311 --> 00:00:42,096
The arrow from the start to
Aarav is his position vector, r.

18
00:00:42,496 --> 00:00:46,081
In symbols, r equals x i hat plus y j hat.

19
00:00:46,081 --> 00:00:49,481
i hat points along x, and j hat along y.

20
00:00:50,131 --> 00:00:52,033
Now, onto the motion notebook.

21
00:00:52,383 --> 00:00:53,977
Watch his two shadows.

22
00:00:53,977 --> 00:00:56,964
The x shadow slides four
metres every second.

23
00:00:56,964 --> 00:00:58,819
The y shadow climbs three.

24
00:00:59,219 --> 00:01:00,842
Two straight line motions.

25
00:01:00,842 --> 00:01:02,847
Two straight lines on the graph.

26
00:01:03,247 --> 00:01:04,412
Slow-mo replay.

27
00:01:04,412 --> 00:01:07,036
Freeze him, and draw his velocity.

28
00:01:07,386 --> 00:01:10,670
The blue arrow is v x,
four metres per second.

29
00:01:10,670 --> 00:01:13,015
The violet arrow is v y, three.

30
00:01:13,415 --> 00:01:16,747
His real velocity is the
diagonal that joins them.

31
00:01:16,747 --> 00:01:20,130
Its length is root four
squared plus three squared.

32
00:01:20,130 --> 00:01:22,571
Five metres per second, not seven.

33
00:01:23,221 --> 00:01:24,121
Your turn.

34
00:01:24,099 --> 00:01:27,157
Six metres per second
east, and eight north.

35
00:01:27,157 --> 00:01:28,872
What is the real speed?

36
00:01:28,872 --> 00:01:30,164
Pause and decide.

37
00:01:33,364 --> 00:01:34,264
Ten!

38
00:01:33,894 --> 00:01:35,444
Root of one hundred.

39
00:01:35,444 --> 00:01:37,692
Never just add the two numbers.

40
00:01:38,342 --> 00:01:40,694
Now the rules, one step at a time.

41
00:01:41,044 --> 00:01:41,976
Step one.

42
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:46,602
In a short time, delta t, the
position changes by delta r.

43
00:01:46,602 --> 00:01:49,966
That is delta x i hat plus delta y j hat.

44
00:01:50,716 --> 00:01:51,723
Step two.

45
00:01:51,723 --> 00:01:53,431
Divide by delta t.

46
00:01:53,431 --> 00:01:57,142
The velocity is v x i hat plus v y j hat.

47
00:01:57,892 --> 00:01:58,829
Step three.

48
00:01:58,829 --> 00:02:01,507
The speed is the length of this arrow.

49
00:02:01,507 --> 00:02:03,982
Root v x squared plus v y squared.

50
00:02:04,732 --> 00:02:05,730
Step four.

51
00:02:05,730 --> 00:02:10,939
The direction is the angle theta,
where tan theta equals v y divided by

52
00:02:10,939 --> 00:02:11,839
v x.

53
00:02:12,343 --> 00:02:13,371
Remember this.

54
00:02:13,371 --> 00:02:17,878
Motion in a plane is just two straight
line motions, happening at the same

55
00:02:17,878 --> 00:02:18,778
time.

56
00:02:19,116 --> 00:02:20,672
Now add acceleration.

57
00:02:21,022 --> 00:02:25,540
Aarav flicks a marble sideways,
along x, across a tilted board.

58
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:30,323
The slope pulls it down the board,
along y, with a steady acceleration.

59
00:02:30,323 --> 00:02:31,689
Watch the path bend.

60
00:02:32,089 --> 00:02:34,637
Across the board, the
speed stays the same.

61
00:02:34,637 --> 00:02:36,757
The blue line on the graph is flat.

62
00:02:37,157 --> 00:02:39,541
Down the slope, it keeps speeding up.

63
00:02:39,541 --> 00:02:41,034
The violet line climbs.

64
00:02:41,434 --> 00:02:45,919
And the velocity arrow always follows
the path, not the pull of the slope.

65
00:02:46,569 --> 00:02:49,565
So we use the straight
line equations twice.

66
00:02:49,565 --> 00:02:51,466
Once for x, once for y.

67
00:02:51,816 --> 00:02:52,716
Along x.

68
00:02:52,712 --> 00:02:55,142
v x equals u x plus a x t.

69
00:02:55,142 --> 00:02:58,771
And x equals u x t plus
half a x t squared.

70
00:02:59,521 --> 00:03:00,480
Along y.

71
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:03,082
v y equals u y plus a y t.

72
00:03:03,082 --> 00:03:06,967
And y equals u y t plus
half a y t squared.

73
00:03:07,717 --> 00:03:09,689
Together, the vector form.

74
00:03:09,689 --> 00:03:11,369
v equals u plus a t.

75
00:03:11,369 --> 00:03:14,291
And r equals u t plus half a t squared.

76
00:03:15,041 --> 00:03:16,338
Side by side.

77
00:03:16,338 --> 00:03:18,548
Along x, no acceleration.

78
00:03:18,548 --> 00:03:21,070
Equal distances in equal times.

79
00:03:21,470 --> 00:03:23,524
Along y, there is acceleration.

80
00:03:23,524 --> 00:03:26,641
The gaps grow, in the
ratio one, three, five.

81
00:03:27,241 --> 00:03:28,268
Now you try.

82
00:03:28,268 --> 00:03:30,828
Aarav flicks the marble twice as fast.

83
00:03:30,828 --> 00:03:33,548
Does it take longer to reach the bottom?

84
00:03:33,548 --> 00:03:34,823
Pause and decide.

85
00:03:38,023 --> 00:03:38,923
No!

86
00:03:38,545 --> 00:03:39,531
Same time.

87
00:03:39,531 --> 00:03:42,332
The flick changes only the x motion.

88
00:03:42,332 --> 00:03:44,906
The time down depends only on y.

89
00:03:45,556 --> 00:03:47,292
Now, one worked example.

90
00:03:47,642 --> 00:03:52,311
A particle starts at the origin with
velocity four i hat, and acceleration

91
00:03:52,311 --> 00:03:53,249
two j hat.

92
00:03:53,249 --> 00:03:56,255
Find its position and
speed at three seconds.

93
00:03:56,755 --> 00:03:59,772
Along x, u x is four and a x is zero.

94
00:03:59,772 --> 00:04:02,758
So x is four times three, twelve metres.

95
00:04:03,508 --> 00:04:06,362
Along y, u y is zero and a y is two.

96
00:04:06,362 --> 00:04:10,231
So y is half times two times
three squared, nine metres.

97
00:04:10,981 --> 00:04:12,006
Now velocity.

98
00:04:12,006 --> 00:04:13,252
v x stays four.

99
00:04:13,252 --> 00:04:16,517
v y is two times three,
six metres per second.

100
00:04:17,267 --> 00:04:20,119
Speed is root four
squared plus six squared.

101
00:04:20,119 --> 00:04:23,769
Root fifty two, about seven
point two metres per second.

102
00:04:24,419 --> 00:04:25,884
Now, the exam trap.

103
00:04:26,234 --> 00:04:30,177
Many students put plain numbers
into v equals u plus a t.

104
00:04:30,177 --> 00:04:32,509
Four plus two times three, ten.

105
00:04:32,909 --> 00:04:35,754
But u and a point in different directions.

106
00:04:35,754 --> 00:04:38,849
Solve along x and y
separately, then combine.

107
00:04:38,849 --> 00:04:41,281
The real answer is seven point two.

108
00:04:41,931 --> 00:04:43,398
Where is this asked?

109
00:04:43,398 --> 00:04:47,907
In questions giving u and a as
vectors, asking for position or speed.

110
00:04:48,507 --> 00:04:49,779
Exam level now.

111
00:04:49,779 --> 00:04:54,715
A particle starts at the origin with
velocity six i hat, and acceleration

112
00:04:54,715 --> 00:04:55,771
four j hat.

113
00:04:55,771 --> 00:04:59,220
When y is eight metres,
find x and the speed.

114
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:00,545
Pause and solve.

115
00:05:05,945 --> 00:05:07,193
The answer is B.

116
00:05:07,193 --> 00:05:09,919
Twelve metres, and ten metres per second.

117
00:05:10,419 --> 00:05:14,301
Along y, eight equals half
times four times t squared.

118
00:05:14,301 --> 00:05:15,950
So t is two seconds.

119
00:05:16,450 --> 00:05:19,126
So x is six times two, twelve metres.

120
00:05:19,126 --> 00:05:21,602
And v y is four times two, eight.

121
00:05:22,102 --> 00:05:25,308
Speed is root six squared
plus eight squared, ten.

122
00:05:25,308 --> 00:05:27,549
Option A just added six and eight.

123
00:05:27,549 --> 00:05:28,816
That is the trap.

124
00:05:29,416 --> 00:05:30,876
Here is your recap.

125
00:05:30,876 --> 00:05:32,376
Screenshot this card.

126
00:05:35,576 --> 00:05:38,413
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

127
00:05:38,813 --> 00:05:39,713
One.

128
00:05:39,325 --> 00:05:42,329
Why is four east plus
three north not seven?

129
00:05:43,229 --> 00:05:44,129
Two.

130
00:05:43,748 --> 00:05:46,928
How do you find the
speed from v x and v y?

131
00:05:47,828 --> 00:05:48,728
Three.

132
00:05:48,434 --> 00:05:51,709
Does a faster flick change
the time down a slope?

133
00:05:51,709 --> 00:05:52,609
Why?

134
00:05:53,315 --> 00:05:56,854
Next time: throw one ball
sideways and drop another.

135
00:05:56,854 --> 00:05:58,203
Which lands first?

136
00:05:58,203 --> 00:05:59,491
Projectile motion.
